<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Draža Mihailović</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1893–1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Draža Mihailović was a Yugoslav army officer who led the royalist Chetnik movement in occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and served as minister of war of the government-in-exile. After brief cooperation with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josip-broz-tito">Tito</a>'s Partisans in 1941 his forces fought them, and many Chetnik units collaborated with Italian and German forces. Captured by the communists in 1946, he was tried and executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/draza-mihailovic.jpg" alt="Draža Mihailović" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aleksandar Simić (1923-2007) (remastered by Savasampion) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Draza_Mihailovic,1943.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
